There was nothing to do on #189 in this run, so it is waiting until 2026-11-22T10:00Z.

**Why nothing changed:** this run started because of the push to main 3b912c9..899f641 (#212). That push changes how repo-looper's nightly scan relocks pins, plus its tests, README, PROPOSALS.md and STATE.md. It does not touch looper-scan, the security job, or the memory (`--ram`) and thread (`--threads`) limits this issue gives CodeQL. No new comment on the issue asks for anything either.

**Where the issue stands:** the fix (58cbdbf, a142f91) is merged on main (8180689..72f0d3f, gates docs+build, build pipeline 3083771156 green). The nightlies run the image that has it (cd7d3689) since cloud#82 pinned it. What is still unproven is the done-when: the nightly security jobs running green.

**Next run:**
- **Read the reports.** It reads the 2026-11-22 nightly security summaries of eventbus, stratum, mailbox, llmproxy, redo, kernel, tenantecho and messaging. Each must be a fresh report, with no CodeQL out-of-memory problem and memory peaks under the 12Gi limit.
- **If they pass,** it posts the outcome comment and closes #189.
- **If the reports are still stale,** the issue waits on #210, the bug where a security job that publishes nothing leaves the old report in place.
- **If one still runs out of memory,** it sizes CodeQL from that report's peak and lands again.

The checkpoint reported "2 files changed, 731 insertions" pushed to `looper/looper-189`, although the checkout showed no changes at the start of this run. I did not look at what those files were.
